hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2691","It was narrated that Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād — and there is a report from him from Mujāhid — from ‘Ā’ishah (RA) who said:\n“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while we were in ihrām. When a riding party passed by us, we would lower the cloth over our faces.”\n\nIt was narrated to us by ‘Abdullāh ibn Sa‘īd al-Ashajj, who said: Ibn Idrīs narrated to us, and he said: I heard Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād.\n\nAlso narrated to us by Yūsuf ibn Mūsā, who said: Jarīr narrated to us.\n\nAlso narrated to us by Muḥammad ibn Hishām, who said: Hushaym narrated to us — all of them from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād.\n\nIn Jarīr’s version: “When they had passed by…”\nIn Hushaym’s version: “When they had passed by, we would uncover it.”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
